@startuml
title torc_py Task-Based Parallelism Library - System Architecture

left to right direction

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

legend left
Abbreviations: MPI = Message Passing Interface, SPMD = Single Program Multiple Data
legend

package "Application" {
  [Python Application] as App
  [Example Suite\n(map, callbacks, SPMD, image preprocessing)] as Examples
  database "Image Dataset\n(folders by label)" as ImageData
  database "HDF5 Output" as HDF5
}

package "torc (Python package)" {
  [API Facade] as API
  [Runtime Controller] as Runtime
  [Worker Scheduler] as Scheduler
  [Task Queues\n(one per worker)] as Queues
  [Worker Thread] as Worker1
  [Worker Thread] as Worker2
  [Task Descriptor\n(Future)] as Future
  [Callback Manager] as CallbackMgr
  [Map Executor] as MapExec
  [SPMD Executor] as SpmdExec
  [Stealing Manager] as StealMgr
  [Timer (gettime)] as Timer
  [Query Service\n(worker_id,num_workers,node_id,num_nodes)] as QuerySvc
  [Config Reader\n(TORC_WORKERS, TORC_STEALING,\nTORC_SERVER_YIELDTIME, TORC_WORKER_YIELDTIME)] as Config
}

package "MPI Layer" {
  [mpi4py] as MpiPy
  [MPI Communicator] as MpiComm
}

node "Cluster / Nodes" {
  node "Rank 0 (Primary)" as Rank0 {
    [MPI Process 0] as P0
    frame "Workers (TORC_WORKERS)" {
      [Worker Threads 0..N-1] as W0N
    }
  }
  node "Other Ranks 1..R-1" as OtherRanks {
    [MPI Process 1..R-1] as PRest
    frame "Workers (per process)" {
      [Worker Threads 0..N-1] as WRest
    }
  }
}

' Application to torc
App --> API : uses torc APIs\nsubmit, wait, map, as_completed,\nstart/init/launch/shutdown,\nspmd, enable/disable_stealing,\ngettime, worker/node queries
Examples --> API
Examples --> ImageData
Examples --> HDF5

' API to runtime and executors
API --> Runtime
API --> MapExec
API --> SpmdExec
API --> QuerySvc
API --> Timer
API --> CallbackMgr
API --> StealMgr

' Runtime wiring
Runtime --> Scheduler
Runtime --> Config
Runtime --> MpiPy

' Scheduling and execution
Scheduler --> Queues
Scheduler --> W0N
Scheduler --> WRest
W0N --> Future : produce input()/result()
WRest --> Future

' Callbacks
Future --> CallbackMgr : on completion\n(pass descriptor)

' Map executor uses scheduler
MapExec --> Scheduler

' SPMD executor over MPI
SpmdExec --> MpiPy
MpiPy --> MpiComm
MpiComm -[#blue]-> P0
MpiComm -[#blue]-> PRest

' Stealing across processes
StealMgr --> Scheduler : request/offer tasks
StealMgr --> MpiPy : inter-process steal messages

' Queries
QuerySvc --> Scheduler : worker_id,num_workers
QuerySvc --> MpiPy : node_id,num_nodes

' Timer
Timer --> Runtime : time source

' Processes and workers
Runtime -down-> P0 : launch/activate
Runtime -down-> PRest : activate workers
P0 -down-> W0N
PRest -down-> WRest
Queues -down-> W0N
Queues -down-> WRest

' Config influences runtime behavior
Config -[dashed]-> Scheduler : TORC_WORKERS
Config -[dashed]-> StealMgr : TORC_STEALING
Config -[dashed]-> Runtime : yield times

' Data paths for example workflow
App --> Future : retrieve inputs/results
Examples --> MapExec : map-style tasks
Examples ..> HDF5 : write results

' Constraints and notes
note right of API
Exposed APIs:
- submit(f,*args,qid,callback)
- wait(tasks)
- as_completed(tasks)
- map(f,*seq,chunksize)
- start/init/launch/shutdown
- spmd(f,*args)
- enable_stealing/disable_stealing
- gettime()
- worker_id()/num_workers()
- node_id()/num_nodes()
end note

note bottom of StealMgr
Optional, enabled by TORC_STEALING.
Idle workers steal from other queues.
end note

note bottom of SpmdExec
Runs f on all ranks to support
application-level MPI routines.
end note

note bottom of Future
Holds submitted input and computed result.
Provides input() and result() accessors.
end note

note top of P0
Primary application task runs on rank 0.
end note

' Technology constraints
note as N1
Constraints:
- Imported as Python module "torc"
- Depends on mpi4py and MPI runtime
- Worker execution via Python threads
end note
N1 .. API

@enduml
